From: Chen Minqiang <ptpt52@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: allow querying the MediaTek WDMA receive path

The WDMA used to receive a wireless station's traffic can differ from the
one used to transmit to it. MT7996 receives through the main WED even
when a station uses the second PCIe interface for transmit.

Let hardware offload drivers request the receive path explicitly while
keeping existing forward-path queries on the transmit path. Advertise
the extension so out-of-tree wireless drivers can support older kernels.

Signed-off-by: Chen Minqiang <ptpt52@gmail.com>
---
--- a/include/linux/netdevice.h
+++ b/include/linux/netdevice.h
@@ -941,6 +941,8 @@ struct net_device_path_stack {
 	struct net_device_path	path[NET_DEVICE_PATH_STACK_MAX];
 };
 
+#define NET_DEVICE_PATH_MTK_WDMA_RX
+
 struct net_device_path_ctx {
 	const struct net_device *dev;
 	u8			daddr[ETH_ALEN];
@@ -952,6 +954,8 @@ struct net_device_path_ctx {
 	} vlan[NET_DEVICE_PATH_VLAN_MAX];
 
 	bool			ieee80211;
+	/* Query the receiving WDMA instead of the station's transmit WDMA. */
+	bool			mtk_wdma_rx;
 };
 
 enum tc_setup_type {
